# ─── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/

# ─── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── PlatformIO / embedded build ──────────────────────────
.pio/
*.elf

# Build stamp — regenerated by cyd/tools/gen_build_stamp.py on EVERY `pio run`
# ([SPEC:CXC-BOARD-HW] workstream 0.4).  A build ARTEFACT whose entire value is
# being newer than the last build; committing it would guarantee merge conflicts
# and would make a checked-out fingerprint lie about which build is running.
# The fingerprint -> string MAP (cyd/build_fingerprints.json) IS committed —
# that one is the registry a fleet report resolves against, and it is
# append-only for exactly that reason.
cyd/src/gen/build_stamp.h

# ─── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# ─── Secrets — NEVER COMMIT ───────────────────────────────
# Per-device WiFi/network config (real creds live here; commit the .example instead)
**/wifi_config.h
**/secrets.yaml
**/secrets.yml
**/*.creds
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/.env

# ─── Ray / misc caches ────────────────────────────────────
.ray/
/tmp/

# ─── Generated docs site (mkdocs output) ──────────────────
site/

# ─── PlatformIO / ESP-IDF generated board config ──────────
# (sdkconfig.cyd + sdkconfig.defaults are intentionally tracked; the
#  per-test-env sdkconfigs are build-generated from defaults)
sdkconfig.cyd_dsl_test
sdkconfig.native_dsl
sdkconfig.esp32c3_dsl_test
sdkconfig.qualia_s3_dsl_test
sdkconfig.esp32c3_dsl_test

# ─── Claude local permission config (machine-local, never commit) ──
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.json
# The TIMESTAMPED BACKUPS are the same machine-local content under a DERIVED name, so the
# exact-filename rule above never saw them: three of them were committed in f391600 carrying
# absolute /Users/... paths. Guard the family, not the one filename.
.mcp.json.bak-*
# Per-session canary written/removed by ~/.claude/scripts/session_{start,end}.sh. Ephemeral,
# per-worktree, and NOT repository content — two copies were committed in f391600.
# Depth-independent: a nested checkout (python/.claude/) grows its own.
**/.claude/session_canary.json
logs/

# ─── Session-retrospective metrics store ([SPEC:CXC-RETRO] §5a) ────
# Regenerable derived data — rebuilt by re-injecting session transcripts. Never a source of truth.
# DEPTH-INDEPENDENT ON PURPOSE. A pattern with an embedded '/' is anchored to THIS file's
# directory, so the old `intelligence/retrospective/data/` silently matched nothing the moment
# intelligence/ became compose_projects/intelligence/ — which is how two metrics.db files got
# committed. `**/` keeps the rule true wherever the tree moves next.
**/intelligence/retrospective/data/

# in-repo agent worktrees — must NOT be tracked or walked (they 18x-collide skill discovery)
.claude/worktrees/

# retired top-level deliverables/ path — canonical ledger lives at corpora/deliverables/ (DEFECT-SWEEP-WRITES-DELIVERABLE-LEDGER-TO)
/deliverables/

# ─── BSG blender models (551 MB local-only source assets) ─────────
# Kept on disk, never tracked/pushed (accidental fold-in removed from history).
compose_projects/bsg/resources/blender_models/

# Untitled widget editor scaffolds (empty "New Widget" saves — never track)
untitled-*.compose.yaml

# ─── Session handover records ─────────────────────────────
# David's ruling, 2026-08-13: these are per-machine working artifacts, not
# repository content. Untracked at the tip by the commit that added this rule.
# NOT erased: the content remains in history at b949b1f, e34af47, b26f60f and
# ad8dc89, and on origin/main. Removing it from history would rewrite a
# published branch that four refs descend from — a separate decision.
session_handover/

# Board flash backup IMAGES — multi-MB, reproducible only from the board itself.
# The .sha256 manifests and backups/README.md ARE committed (see that README).
backups/**/*.bin
